<item>
            <title>[ZEPPELIN-6306] Add fail-fast check for JavaCompiler in Java interpreter</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/ZEPPELIN-6306</link>
                <project id="12316221" key="ZEPPELIN">Zeppelin</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Background:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;In the `StaticRepl` class , &lt;tt&gt;ToolProvider.getSystemJavaCompiler()&lt;/tt&gt; is used to obtain a compiler instance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;This works only in a JDK environment; in a JRE, it returns &lt;tt&gt;null&lt;/tt&gt;, which can lead to errors later in the execution flow.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;During a recent refactoring review, it was suggested to perform a null check at the earliest point to implement a &lt;b&gt;fail-fast&lt;/b&gt; mechanism.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Proposed Solution:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Move the initialization of &lt;tt&gt;JavaCompiler compiler = ToolProvider.getSystemJavaCompiler();&lt;/tt&gt; to the very beginning of the method.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;If &lt;tt&gt;compiler&lt;/tt&gt; is &lt;tt&gt;null&lt;/tt&gt;, throw a clear exception (&lt;tt&gt;Exception&lt;/tt&gt;) with a message explaining that a JDK is required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;


&lt;p&gt;&#160;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
